          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Nikki\",\"addressee\":\"Keith\",\"anchor_quote\":\"I love you\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"Nikki directly avows her loving emotional state toward Keith. The narration explicitly characterizes the utterance as an honest admission, so truth-state presentation is its clearest core force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"I love you\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"The admission felt like a release, a moment of pure honesty that left them both vulnerable but deeply connected.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.96,\"reason\":\"Nikki does not undertake a future action, obligation, or defined relational commitment in the focal expression. It is an avowal of present feeling; no promise by Nikki should be inferred from the intimacy, Keith's reciprocation, or their discussion of not saying goodbye.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"I love you\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.94,\"reason\":\"The expression is also represented as a spontaneous affective discharge: Nikki says it suddenly, before she can inhibit it, and experiences it as a release. This gives it substantial expressive force beyond its assertive avowal.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"“I love you,” she said suddenly, the words spilling out before she could stop them.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"The admission felt like a release\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"reason\":\"The focal expression's core force is adequately represented by avowal and spontaneous emotional expression. The supplied evidence does not establish a distinct residual function such as a request, command, apology, or greeting.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"I love you\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"Nikki says this to Keith while they are lying together after an intimate encounter. The words arise suddenly while she feels emotionally full; Keith pauses, smiles, and reciprocates.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The focal utterance contains no identifiable undertaking by Nikki. Keith receives it as a love admission and reciprocates with “I love you too,” but that uptake does not convert Nikki's avowal into a promise or commitment.\",\"recognised_work\":false,\"recognition_note\":\"I do not recognize the supplied passage as a particular previously known work.\",\"limitations\":\"The scene strongly supports the represented sincerity and spontaneity of this occurrence, but the focal words alone do not specify any formal relationship status, future obligation, or durable commitment.\"}"
        }
